"Let $\\mathcal{C}_{1},\\mathcal{C}_{2} \\subset \\mathbb{P}^{2}_{\\mathbb{C}}$ be two $d$-arrangements for a fixed $d\\geqslant 1$. Let $G_{1}$ and $G_{2}$ be their associated Levi graphs. **Generalized Terao conjecture.** If $G_{1}$ and $G_{2}$ are isomorphic and $\\mathcal{C}_{1}$ is free, then $\\mathcal{C}_{2}$ is also free.\n\nThis asks whether freeness of a $d$-arrangement is determined by the isomorphism class of its Levi graph, extending Terao's conjecture from line arrangements to arrangements of curves. The source presents it as a question, and no resolution is supplied here."